subsequent MLX changes are maintained independently in this repository.

MiniMax H3 model weights are not included. They are distributed separately
under the MiniMax H3 Community License Agreement.

Optional LTX 2.3 support integrates the MIT-licensed dgrauet/ltx-2-mlx
packages as pinned, separately installed runtime dependencies:
https://github.com/dgrauet/ltx-2-mlx

Lightricks/LTX-2 was consulted as a technical reference. Its source and model
weights are not vendored here.
https://github.com/Lightricks/LTX-2

H3SteelAttentionSource.swift and H3UnfencedSteelAttentionSource.swift embed
MIT-licensed MLX Steel primitives and indexed/dense attention adaptations from
Apple Inc. The complete MIT notice is retained in those files and in the
packaged native worker notices.
https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx-swift/tree/901941965d82e4a216d4d117231d847d194c563d

Pika-Labs/Pika-H3-Flex was consulted for native H3 Flex adapter and sampling
contracts at revision 4bf8ea508891a432106e70f675d287c27f02306d:
https://github.com/Pika-Labs/Pika-H3-Flex
The Swift implementation is maintained independently. Pika weights and the
MiniMax H3 base are distributed separately under their publisher's terms;
weights and third-party runtime source are not included here.

The optional native TAELTX2.3 Standard/Wide preview decoder was independently
implemented from Ollin Boer Bohan's MIT-licensed architecture and checkpoint
contracts, consulted at revision 32ac0146b11007cda5a57b60a3b35653361fb8a4:
https://github.com/madebyollin/taehv
The full notice is retained in integrations/weetodd-mlx/Notices/TAELTX.txt and
packaged native LTX worker notices. Preview weights are downloaded separately;
they are not included in the application or this repository.
